          <Pad Id="uG6B3ZHhomi58CcI8Z41BY" Bounds="85,85,520,110" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Input (Int) [Qt]&#xD;&#xA;- Number field with +/- buttons&#xD;&#xA;- Channel: binds the value, the user writes back&#xD;&#xA;- Min, Max: default is the full int range, or the Min/Max attributes of the channel&#xD;&#xA;- Value: current value; Bang: true for one frame when the user changed it">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="wexoLSl6gDNzIvacn77pEl" Bounds="85,879,830,126" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- A plain value or an IOBox on Channel is the start value and sets the value from the patch.&#xD;&#xA;- A typed value goes out on Enter (the field keeps the focus) or when the field loses focus, e.g. by a click or tap anywhere else in the window; Esc discards it and leaves the field.&#xD;&#xA;- +/-, the arrow keys and the mouse wheel change the value at once. If the patch and the user change it in the same frame, the user wins.&#xD;&#xA;- Labels are not part of the input: wrap it in a Labeled element (here a Column stacks the Labeled inputs).">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
